All-American Hustle
===================

A modified Paintown beat-'em-up project built around custom characters, custom stages, persistent RPG progression, and an AI/rendered animation workflow.

Windows quick start
-------------------
1. Install Python 3 if it is not already available.
2. Run `run_game.bat` from the repository root.
3. The launcher validates the game files, enables the RPG script on every Paintown stage, then launches `All American Hustle.exe`.

Progression
-----------
Persistent state is saved outside the game directory so installs remain portable:
- Windows: `%APPDATA%\\AllAmericanHustle\\save.json`
- Other systems: `~/.all_american_hustle/save.json`

The RPG layer tracks level, XP, health, attack/defense scaling, currency, inventory, quests, and rewards.

AI/rendered animation import
----------------------------
Put an ordered PNG sequence in a folder, then run for example:

`python tools/import_animation.py JohnDutch attack1 C:\\frames\\attack1 --key key_attack1 --range 60 --damage 5`

The importer renames/copies frames into the selected Paintown player action folder and updates or creates the corresponding `(anim ...)` block in the character definition. Existing attacks can still be hand-tuned afterward for exact hit boxes and offsets.

Validation
----------
Run:

`python tools/self_test.py`

and:

`python tools/prepare_game.py`

The repository also contains a GitHub Actions validation workflow.

Engine note
-----------
This repository contains a prebuilt Paintown-based Windows runtime and game data. The root CMake project prepares/packages that runtime; it does not pretend to compile nonexistent local Paintown C++ sources.
